<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Le Verger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1488">1488</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Treaty of Sablé · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mad-war">Mad War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Le Verger, also called the Treaty of Sablé, was signed in August 1488 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-viii-of-france">Charles VIII of France</a> and Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> of Brittany after the Breton defeat at Saint-Aubin-du-Cormier. Francis had to dismiss his foreign troops, hand over several towns as pledges and promise not to marry his daughters without the king's consent. He died weeks later, and his daughter Anne's marriage to Charles VIII brought Brittany under French rule.</p></div>
